In article <1991Nov12.012411.3830@kakwa.ucs.ualberta.ca> piebia@ee.ualberta.ca (Edward Piebiak) writes:
>I would like to know if anyone one out there is haveing any problems getting
>nethack (3.0j) to work on a Mac running sys 7.0.1.  The game would run
>with different fonts (ie. the hallways would be a null char instead of a
># char.) and it would scroll messages _REALLY_ slowly.  Worse than if I
>was playing over a 2400bps line.

     I've had no problems running the NetHack 3.0j3+ binary distributed on
linc.cis.upenn.edu with System 7.0.1.  The screen display seems just fine.
(Note that walls and hallways and so on do look different in Mac NetHack than
they do in versions played over ASCII terminals; this is not a bug.
     My bet would be that it's some sort of INIT conflict (though I use a dozen
or so INITs and cdevs and I don't have any problems).
